course: dictionary
lesson: 2843
title: Short words with many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some short words are cut down from longer ones, and one short word can stand for several long words. «Doc» can mean doctor, document or documentary. You cannot tell which one from the word alone, so read the words around it.
explain: When someone says «Thanks, doc», they are talking to a doctor. When someone says «Send me the doc», they mean a computer file. Ask yourself: who is speaking, and what are they talking about? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Cartoons can be tricky too. Bugs Bunny munches a carrot and asks «What's up, Doc?», but that is a cartoon. A real wild rabbit fills up on grass, clover and leafy plants, and carrots are only a small sugary treat. So a cartoon can be funny without being a true picture of real life.
fact: Doc is an informal word, which means it is used in everyday talk and not in formal writing.
fact: «Doc» is short for doctor, when you speak to one: «Thanks, doc.»
fact: «Doc» is short for document, especially a computer file: «Send me the doc.»
fact: «Doc» can also be short for a documentary film, which is a true film about real things.
fact: Context clues, such as who is speaking and what they are talking about, help you choose the right meaning.
exercise: In «Send me the doc», what does doc most likely mean? | A doctor who helps sick people | A film about nature | A cartoon rabbit | *A document, such as a computer file
exercise: «Thanks, doc», said Ava as the nurse handed her a sticker. What does doc mean here? | *A doctor | A computer file | A document | A documentary film
exercise: Bugs Bunny munches a carrot in the cartoon. What does the sentence tell you about wild rabbits and carrots? | Wild rabbits never eat plants | Carrots are their main food | *Carrots are only a small sugary treat, and grass and clover are their main food | Carrots and clover are the same thing
test: A shared doc is a | A kind of sweet carrot | *A computer file that people can work on together | A visit to a doctor shared by a family | A famous cartoon line
test: «Dad read the doc and found the rules.» Which meaning fits best? | *A document with written rules | A doctor | A rabbit in a cartoon | A documentary about rules
exam: «Doc» is short for three longer words. Which one is NOT one of them? | Doctor | Document | *Dinosaur | Documentary
